# Kampi.fun platform rules

- TypeScript strict mode with `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`; avoid `any`.
- Apps import packages only — never import across apps.
- Server is authoritative for all game and wallet outcomes.
- Store chips as integers/BigInt; expose as strings in JSON when needed.
- Every wallet mutation requires a unique idempotency key.
- Use Zod schemas from `@kampi/contracts` for shared messages and env validation.
- Do not add real-money, KYC, or cash-out functionality in this phase.
- Do not hard-code secrets; use `.env` and `.env.example`.
- Prefer focused changes; match existing patterns in each app/package.
- Run `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, and `pnpm test` before claiming work is done.
